<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - Hungary T-bill yields seen falling.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Hungary T-bill yields seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yields on Hungarian discount Treasury bills were mostly seen dropping at this week's auctions as inflation continued to decline and market liquidity improved substantially since December, dealers said.</p>
<p>The State Debt Management Centre will auction one-month T-bills on Tuesday, three-month T-bills on Wednesday, six-month bills on Thursday and 12-month bills on Friday.</p>
<p> T-BILLS	  ONE-MONTH   THREE-MONTH   SIX-MONTH    12-MONTH</p>
<p>Bills offered</p>
<p>   (HUF billion)    1		5	     12	     14 @</p>
<p>Average yield at</p>
<p>   last auction    21.84	  22.08	  21.74	  21.46</p>
<p>Valid bid</p>
<p>   range     19.84-22.84  20.08-22.58  19.74-22.24  19.46-21.96</p>
<p>FORECASTS OF HUNGARIAN DEALERS</p>
<p>Istvan Halasz/Bank Austria Girocredit</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	  21.85	  21.35	  21	     20.95</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	  22	     21.5	   21.2	   21.1</p>
<p>Gabor Pozsgay/Creditanstalt Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	  22	     22.3	   21.4	   20.95</p>
<p>    MAXIMUM	  22.05	  22.35	  21.5	   21.05</p>
<p>Zsolt Bango/Gog Securities</p>
<p>    AVERAGE	  21.5	   21.13	  20.9	   20.85</p>
